scale at their doctor's office. New research shows that BMI, the body mass index we've relied on for

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.140
decades, misclassifies more than one-third of adults when compared directly against precise DXA

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.260
body composition scans. The study took a large group of adults and ran them through both the

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.740
standard BMI calculation and advanced dual energy x-ray absorb geometry scans that actually measure

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:49.780
fat mass, lean mass, and bone. The results were striking, more than one-third of participants ended

